const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文在美国样本中检验公司资产增长与后续股票收益的横截面关系。 阅读时应把它理解为受样本、时点和制度限定的问题，而不是可以脱离条件的结论。",en:"The article tests the cross-sectional relation between firm asset growth and subsequent stock returns in a U.S. sample. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2008.01370.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它将年度资产增长与其他已记录收益决定因素比较，会计构造、组合时点和基准收益定义均至关重要。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中一项，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It compares annual firm asset-growth rates with other documented return determinants, making accounting construction, portfolio timing, and benchmark-return definition central. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2008.01370.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"输入包括时点总资产与财务报表、财年与申报日期、证券收益和退市、公司样本、会计调整和形成日期。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原研究分别记录，不能仅因变量同名或使用最新修订值就视为可比。",en:"Inputs include point-in-time total assets and financial statements, fiscal and filing dates, security returns and delistings, firm universe, accounting adjustments, and formation dates. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2008.01370.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"摘要报告年度资产增长在样本中的历史预测能力，不把任何资产负债表扩张变成确定的异常收益。 它只支持来源所描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The abstract reports historical predictive ability of annual asset growth in its sample; it does not turn any balance-sheet expansion into a certain abnormal return. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2008.01370.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"使用披露可得性而非最新重述数据；定义资产增长、并购、货币和合并口径；纳入退市并在持有期前冻结组合。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Use publication availability rather than latest restated data; define asset growth, mergers, currency, and consolidation; retain delistings and freeze portfolios before holding periods. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2008.01370.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The Journal of Finance (2008)。会计制度、融资条件和交易成本不同，历史横截面不构成当前排序、估值判断或可执行组合。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The Journal of Finance (2008). Accounting regimes, financing conditions, and trading costs vary, so this historical cross-section is not a current ranking, valuation judgment, or executable portfolio. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2008.01370.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2008) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Asset Growth and the Cross-Section of Stock Returns”公开说明的研究对象与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。会计制度、融资条件和交易成本不同，历史横截面不构成当前排序、估值判断或可执行组合。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Asset Growth and the Cross-Section of Stock Returns”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
